  "worked_solution": "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $P\u2261\\text{T}$ and $Q\u2261\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00ac(P\u2228Q) & \u2261\u00ac(\\text{T}\u2228\\text{T}) \\\\  & \u2261\u00ac\\text{T} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P\u2261\\text{T}$ and $Q\u2261\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00acP\u2228Q & \u2261\u00ac\\text{T}\u2228\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\u2228\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P\u2261\\text{F}$ and $Q\u2261\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00ac(P\u2228Q) & \u2261\u00ac(\\text{F}\u2228\\text{F}) \\\\  & \u2261\u00ac\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,\u00ac(P\u2228Q)\\,$ | $\\,\u00acP\u2228Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $\u00ac(P\u2228Q)$ is logically equivalent to $\u00acP\u2228Q,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are *different* (one is $\\text{F},\\text{F},\\text{F},\\text{T}$, while the other is $\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{T}$). Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\u00ac(P\u2228Q)\\text{\u29f8}\u2262\u00acP\u2228Q.\n$$",
